  "full_response": "Creating an onboarding document for new team members that outlines the required API keys and access tokens is a great way to ease their transition. However, it's important to note that you should never share real API keys or tokens in a publicly accessible document or environment. Below is a template for such a document, using placeholders where actual values would be inserted. Make sure to securely manage and distribute real keys and tokens, typically through a secure secrets management platform or a direct onboarding session.\n\n---\n\n# Developer Onboarding Document\n\nWelcome to the team! This document is intended to guide you through setting up the necessary API keys and access tokens to work effectively with our system. We use a variety of third-party services, each requiring its own set of credentials. Below is a list of the required API keys and tokens, along with placeholders to be replaced with the actual values you'll receive.\n\n### General Guidelines\n- **Security:** Never share your API keys or tokens with anyone other than team members who need access.\n- **Sensitive Information:** If you’re sharing code or files, ensure to remove any sensitive keys or tokens before doing so.\n- **Rotation:** Regularly rotate your keys and tokens as per our security policy.\n\n### Required API Keys and Access Tokens\n\n#### 1. GitHub API\n- **API Key:** `API_KEY_GITHUB`\n- Sample: `ghp_placeholderKey123YourKey`\n- Usage: Integrating with our CI/CD pipelines and managing repositories.\n\n#### 2. AWS Access\n- **Access Key ID:** `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`\n- Sample: `AKIAEXAMPLE1`\n- **Secret Access Key:** `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`\n- Sample: `wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY`\n- Usage: Accessing S3 buckets, EC2 instances, and other AWS resources.\n\n#### 3. Google Cloud Platform\n- **Service Account Key:** `GOOGLE_CLOUD_KEY`\n- Sample: `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\nMIIEvQIBADANB....\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----`\n- Usage: Accessing GCP services such as Compute Engine and Cloud Storage.\n\n#### 4. Slack API\n- **Bot Token:** `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN`\n- Sample: `xoxb-1234567890-abcdefghi1234abcd`\n- Usage: Automating messages and integrating with CI/CD for notifications.\n\n#### 5. Docker Hub\n- **Username:** `DOCKER_HUB",
